{"id":"05ef2f5d5e24b0d655d451e406e0208008863866","axis":"silent","repo":"cypress-io/cypress","sha":"05ef2f5d5e24b0d655d451e406e0208008863866","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"cli/CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@"," - Fixed a regression in [16.0.0](#16-0-0) where `<video>` and `<audio>` elements in Chromium-based browsers could not load their metadata or start playing until the whole media file had downloaded. With a large file, such as a progressive MP4 served from a CDN, the element stayed at `readyState` 0 and tests that waited on it timed out. Setting `forceHttp1: true` worked around the issue. Fixed in [#35389](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/pull/35389)."," - [`.type()`](https://on.cypress.io/type) now moves the caret of a `url` input as it types, and starts typing at a caret position your app set with `setSelectionRange()`. For example, after `.type('{leftArrow}{leftArrow}{leftArrow}')` on a `url` input holding `https://www.example.com`, the input's `selectionStart` is now `20` instead of staying at `23`. Fixed in [#35465](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/pull/35465)."," - [`.type()`](https://on.cypress.io/type) now accepts consecutive `{upArrow}` and `{downArrow}` sequences, such as `{upArrow}{upArrow}`, on `date`, `month`, `week`, `time`, and `datetime-local` inputs, and steps the value once per arrow. Previously, a single arrow worked but more than one in a row failed with an error saying the input required a valid date, month, week, time, or datetime. Fixed in [#35352](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/pull/35352).","+- Fixed an issue where, when the application under test was on a different origin than the one the test started on, such as within [`cy.origin()`](https://on.cypress.io/origin), `document.cookie` returned `HttpOnly` cookies and could overwrite or delete them. `document.cookie` now behaves as it does in the browser: it does not return `HttpOnly` cookies, and cannot set, change, or delete them. Fixed in [#35283](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/pull/35283).","+- Fixed an issue where [`cy.request()`](https://on.cypress.io/request) and [`cy.visit()`](https://on.cypress.io/visit) kept sending a cookie while following redirects after a response in the chain had deleted it, which could make a server redirect repeatedly until `maxRedirects` was reached. Each redirect now sends only the cookies the browser has for that URL, so cookies for the first host are no longer sent to a different host. A `Cookie` header passed in `headers` is now kept on redirects to the same host, and is no longer sent on a redirect to a different host. Fixes [#34901](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/34901)."," - Fixed an issue where a request for a Cypress-reserved path that Cypress does not serve, such as `/__/does-not-exist` or `/__cypress/does-not-exist`, never received a response. A `fetch()` or `<script>` load for such a path hung until the page's own timeout, and [`cy.request()`](https://on.cypress.io/request) failed after 30 seconds with \"No response was received within the timeout.\" These requests now receive a `404` promptly, so a synchronous `XMLHttpRequest` to one no longer freezes the browser. Fixes [#34810](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/34810) and [#35026](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/35026)."," - Fixed an issue where, in `cypress run` with the Electron browser and video disabled, the first screenshot in a spec, including the screenshot taken when a test fails, made the application under test render far more slowly for the rest of that spec. Fixes [#35291](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/35291)."," - Fixed a regression in [8.4.0](#8-4-0) where `.scrollTo()` on a scrollable element wrapped with [`Cypress.$`](https://on.cypress.io/$), other than the window or `body`, threw `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'slice')` when given a selector string, a number, or `'max'`, such as `Cypress.$('#list').scrollTo('#item')` or `Cypress.$('#list').scrollTo(120)`. It now scrolls to the matching element or position. Fixed in [#35460](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/pull/35460)."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/driver/cypress/e2e/e2e/origin/cookie_misc.cy.ts","lines":["@@ -301,6 +301,59 @@ describe('misc cookie tests', { browser: '!webkit' }, () => {","     })","   })"," ","+  describe('document.cookie with HttpOnly cookies', () => {","+    beforeEach(() => {","+      cy.visit(`https://www.foobar.com:3502/fixtures/primary-origin.html`)","+      cy.visit(`https://app.foobar.com:3503/fixtures/secondary-origin.html`)","+      cy.origin(`https://app.foobar.com:3503`, () => {","+        cy.window().then((win) => {","+          return cy.wrap(win.fetch(`/set-cookie?cookie=foo=bar; Path=/; HttpOnly`))","+        })","+","+        cy.reload()","+      })","+    })","+","+    it('does not read HttpOnly cookies', () => {","+      cy.origin(`https://app.foobar.com:3503`, () => {","+        cy.document().its('cookie').should('not.include', 'foo=')","+        cy.getCookie('foo').its('value').should('eq', 'bar')","+      })","+    })","+","+    const writes = ['foo=changed; Path=/', 'foo=changed', 'foo=; Path=/; Max-Age=0', 'foo=; Max-Age=0']","+","+    writes.forEach((cookie) => {","+      it(`does not replace or expire HttpOnly cookies with \"${cookie}\"`, () => {","+        cy.origin(`https://app.foobar.com:3503`, { args: { cookie } }, ({ cookie }) => {","+          cy.window().then((win) => {","+            win.document.cookie = cookie","+            // the second write landing means the first has been handled","+            win.document.cookie = 'sync=1; Path=/'","+          })","+","+          cy.getCookie('sync').should('exist')","+","+          cy.getCookie('foo').should('include', { value: 'bar', httpOnly: true })","+        })","+      })","+    })","+","+    it('does not set cookies marked HttpOnly', () => {","+      cy.origin(`https://app.foobar.com:3503`, () => {","+        cy.window().then((win) => {","+          win.document.cookie = 'baz=qux; Path=/; HttpOnly'","+          win.document.cookie = 'sync=1; Path=/'","+        })","+","+        cy.getCookie('sync').should('exist')","+","+        cy.getCookie('baz').should('be.null')","+        cy.document().its('cookie').should('not.include', 'baz=')","+      })","+    })","+  })","+","   describe('Same-Site Cross-Origin cookie behavior', () => {","     const cookie = 'foo1=bar2'","     const site = 'foobar.com'"],"additions":53,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/proxy/lib/adapters/copy-cookies-from-response.ts","lines":["@@ -13,11 +13,12 @@ function setSimulatedCookies (mw: ResponseInterceptionMiddlewareCtx) {","   if (mw.res.wantsInjection !== 'fullCrossOrigin') return"," ","   const defaultDomain = (new URL(mw.req.proxiedUrl)).hostname","-  const allCookiesForRequest = mw.getCookieJar()","+","+  mw.simulatedCookies = mw.getCookieJar()","   .getCookies(mw.req.proxiedUrl)","   .map((cookie) => toughCookieToAutomationCookie(cookie, defaultDomain))","-","-  mw.simulatedCookies = allCookiesForRequest","+  // document.cookie never reads HttpOnly values; it only needs to know they exist so it can't replace them","+  .map((cookie) => (cookie.httpOnly ? { ...cookie, value: '' } : cookie))"," }"," "," /**"],"additions":4,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/proxy/lib/adapters/set-injection-level.ts","lines":["@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ export async function setInjectionLevel (mw: ResponseInterceptionMiddlewareCtx):"," ","   mw.res.isInitial = mw.req.cookies['__cypress.initial'] === 'true'"," ","+  if (!mw.req.isFileServerRequest) {","+    delete mw.incomingRes.headers['x-cypress-file-server-error']","+  }","+","   const isHTML = resContentTypeIs(mw.incomingRes, 'text/html')","   const isRenderedHTML = reqWillRenderHtml(mw.req, mw.incomingRes)"," "],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/proxy/lib/http/request-middleware.ts","lines":